      "problem": "Calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for $y=3{x}^{4}+\\frac{7}{{x}^{4}}-12x.$",
      "worked_solution": "Here, we apply the addition, constant multiple, and power rules:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3{x}^{4}+\\frac{7}{{x}^{4}}-12x) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3{x}^{4})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(7{x}^{-4})-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(12x) \\\\  & =3\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{4})+7\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{-4})-12\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x) \\\\  & =3\\cdot 4{x}^{(4-1)}+7\\cdot (-4){x}^{(-4-1)}-12\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =12{x}^{3}-28{x}^{-5}-12 \\\\  & =12{x}^{3}-\\frac{28}{{x}^{5}}-12\\end{aligned}\n$$",
